1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,260
One dream.

2
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:04,660
One wish.

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:08,260
If you want it, gotta go over the top.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,680
Setting sail and heading for the unknown.

5
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:33,380
Cutting through the
winds and waves as I go.

6
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,437
Gotta keep it up, never stopping, no.

7
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,837
Cause I'm aiming to get there first, yeah.

8
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:41,417
It's all or nothing, no time to worry.

9
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,160
Do it later, right now I'm living free.

10
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:51,477
When your foes look like
they will overwhelm you.

11
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:56,380
It means your heart's saying
this is what you can't do.

12
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:59,537
Despite all that to run is not an option.

13
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:01,637
Once they're closed, I
feel the satisfaction.

14
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,937
You think I'm rude,
here's my appreciation.

15
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:07,040
When things are getting
tough, just gotta smile.

16
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:12,317
If you are going on your way.

17
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,577
And you're looking for
a fresh, brand new day.

18
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:17,737
Then make sure your only
thought you have is.

19
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:19,257
Yes, I can.

20
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:22,057
As you're on your way.

21
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:24,337
Marked maps will be made.

22
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:27,197
Yes, with every step that you will take.

23
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:30,397
Just look at all you've been through.

24
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:32,137
Look ahead at new horizons.

25
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:33,977
In view shining brightly.

26
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:36,860
Oh, who knows what's waiting for you.

27
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:40,117
Dream living, that's the way.

28
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:42,197
Make like a hurricane.

29
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:45,100
Now, got to make your mark today.

30
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:51,177
One dream, one wish.

31
00:01:51,260 --> 00:01:52,997
Your dreams don't run away.

32
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,917
Go for the knockout.

33
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,100
Over the top!

34
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:02,220
Darkstorm, there you are.

35
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:03,836
Where have you been?

36
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:06,660
Is there something wrong, Kin'emon?

37
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:08,392
There's a problem afoot.

38
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:15,035
The enemy has learned of our
fire and mark of the moon?

39
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:17,260
Afraid so.

40
00:02:17,460 --> 00:02:19,520
We're into Major Hot Water now.

41
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:21,978
How can we even fix this mess, Duke?

42
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:25,336
We took such care to be safe
when we distributed them.

43
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,588
How in the world did
they foil us like this?

44
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:31,857
We even chose this
coded symbol and the off

45
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:34,411
chance that it fell into unintended hands.

46
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:37,277
I can't imagine how
they were able to decode

47
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:39,937
our message and learn
of the tattoo's meaning.

48
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:42,420
Where could we possibly have gone wrong?

49
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:45,060
And our problems don't end there.

50
00:02:46,220 --> 00:02:48,497
There are reports that
our allies in the capital

51
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:51,286
were apprehended by Kaido
and Orochi's forces.

52
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:54,460
You're under arrest!

53
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:59,040
There's no use resisting.

54
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:00,358
We know everything.

55
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:04,280
Look what he had.

56
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:07,440
You think you're smart, huh?

57
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:08,560
Check it out.

58
00:03:08,780 --> 00:03:10,460
He's got the moon tattoo.

59
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:15,060
Those who bear that mark are
considered traitors to the Shogun.

60
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:16,010
You hear?

61
00:03:16,093 --> 00:03:18,020
You are to report all rebels.

62
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:25,100
Word travels fast.

63
00:03:25,700 --> 00:03:28,465
Everyone in the capital
must have heard by now.

64
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:32,220
We have little to no time to
patrol the city's bathhouses.

65
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:34,520
Lucky you.

66
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:37,226
And what do you mean by that?

67
00:03:43,540 --> 00:03:46,117
Only Stealth Black could
have pulled that off.

68
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:47,760
I'll get him next time.

69
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:52,259
You were there too, if I recall, so
don't pin all of that mess on me.

70
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:17,820
Sir Kyoshiro, I'm afraid that
Komorosaki's wake has been cancelled.

71
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:22,360
We feared chaos would ensue with a
crowd of this size in attendance.

72
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:30,184
It's expected that even more people will
show up for the funeral tomorrow as well.

73
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:35,924
Please take extra caution, sir.

74
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:38,917
This tragedy has caused
unrest among the people.

75
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,176
They may resent you for your actions.

76
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,296
Of course they will.

77
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:44,540
They don't get it.

78
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:52,740
Unfortunately, there was no other way.

79
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:59,340
Besides, I'm the one who suffered the
greatest loss here Where's my pity party?

80
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:01,280
Of course, sir.

81
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:09,137
I spoke to the Shogun.

82
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:11,117
The man's absolutely furious.

83
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:13,337
Can't blame him, though?

84
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:15,560
He's got this to fear.

85
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:27,737
We're supposed to be friends, aren't we?

86
00:05:27,820 --> 00:05:29,020
So talk it out.

87
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:30,820
Knock it off already.

88
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:37,262
Allies keep getting caught before we even
get a chance to see our plan take flight.

89
00:05:37,620 --> 00:05:41,160
It's been happening ever since
your crew compromised us.

90
00:05:41,700 --> 00:05:43,120
What are you implying?

91
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:45,577
That white bear and his friends talked.

92
00:05:45,660 --> 00:05:48,836
How else would the enemy
forces know of our plan, huh?

93
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:52,582
My crew would sooner die
than rat out our allies.

94
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:54,720
So watch your mouth!

95
00:05:56,720 --> 00:06:00,000
Wait, this is exactly
what they want, Traffy.

96
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:02,577
Why don't you mind your
own business, Blackleg?

97
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:04,020
I'll make the call.

98
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:07,133
Slow down and cool your heads, you guys.

99
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:11,955
I don't think my head is the one you
should be worrying about right now.

100
00:06:12,460 --> 00:06:16,220
In times like these, it's
important to trust your friends.

101
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:17,517
Are you serious?

102
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:20,129
You're the least
trustworthy person I know!

103
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,157
I, uh, didn't see anything.

104
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:28,697
That's the most jacked
up face I've ever seen.

105
00:06:28,780 --> 00:06:30,368
It's what you get, I guess.

106
00:06:31,420 --> 00:06:33,080
Just where are you going?

107
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:36,137
You must sever ties with
those who were captured

108
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:39,560
Your friends are dead to
us now What'd you say?

109
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:44,240
A ninja knows when to cut their
losses You're scaring me, Shinobu!

110
00:06:48,420 --> 00:06:54,040
This isn't some child's game we're
playing here, you know It's been so long.

111
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:58,880
This is it.

112
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:02,140
We have waited 20 years for this.

113
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:06,320
If we fail this time, there
will be no second chances.

114
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:13,020
Control yourself, Shinobu.

115
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:16,500
I'm sorry, Master Khan.

116
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:20,537
Things will not always go as we had hoped.

117
00:07:20,620 --> 00:07:22,940
I understand your frustration,

118
00:07:23,300 --> 00:07:27,817
but without the help of these people whose
goals miraculously align with our own,

119
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:28,841
we'd be nowhere.

120
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:31,060
We must all work together.

121
00:07:31,460 --> 00:07:33,400
Fulfill Lord Odin's wish.

122
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:36,750
Hello!

123
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:38,620
Party's here!

124
00:07:39,940 --> 00:07:43,137
I couldn't help but overhear
you from outside the window.

125
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:46,877
And oh boy, you folks have
some nice pipes, I tell ya.

126
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:47,800
Hang on a sec.

127
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:49,080
Who even are you?

128
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:53,100
Oh, wow, what a beauty.

129
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:55,106
Are you some kind of goddess?

130
00:07:56,740 --> 00:07:58,920
Aw, aren't you sweet? Come on in.

131
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:01,780
Well, don't mind if I do. Thank you.

132
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:08,620
I know you, Yoshinobu.

133
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:13,160
Yes, and you, Kanjuro, right?

134
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:16,000
Would you look at that?

135
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:18,257
Seems like you're the real deal.

136
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:22,752
I'm relieved, as I got an invite to a
special event, if you catch my drift.

137
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:26,160
This is all the rage
in the capital, I hear.

138
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:29,780
I'm getting a little
starstruck, truth be told.

139
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:31,960
So lay it on me, chief.

140
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:34,640
Is there a big battle of Bruin?

141
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:52,580
That's my sword.

142
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:54,120
My sword!

143
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:01,620
Wait a sec.

144
00:09:01,940 --> 00:09:04,020
You really scared me!

145
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:07,600
Please, we need to rest.

146
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:11,340
We don't want that wound opening up.

147
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,820
You gotta listen to it and go back to bed!

148
00:09:16,280 --> 00:09:17,400
Where am I?

149
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:29,297
If it weren't for your assistance, I fear
that we might have died earlier today.

150
00:09:29,380 --> 00:09:30,800
You have my gratitude.

151
00:09:33,700 --> 00:09:35,520
Thanks a bunch, mister!

152
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:40,080
You suffered a terrible
wound on our behalf.

153
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:41,540
I'm sorry.

154
00:09:41,980 --> 00:09:44,274
I hope I can make it up to you somehow.

155
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:49,257
No, it was my own fault
that I got hurt like this.

156
00:09:49,340 --> 00:09:51,760
You two had nothing to do with any of it.

157
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:55,520
I gotta find that guy.

158
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:56,957
Where the hell did he go?

159
00:09:57,040 --> 00:09:59,940
That jackass still has my shoes wet! No!

160
00:10:00,380 --> 00:10:02,717
If you don't stay and
recover, you could die!

161
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:03,840
Ah, come on!

162
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:07,117
That's the shoulder that got
stabbed, you freakin' idiot!

163
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:09,260
My apologies! I'm leaving!

164
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:11,560
Don't try to stop me!

165
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:13,837
Stay a bit longer?

166
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:16,020
just until the pain goes away.

167
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:18,831
Ugh, you're the one who's causing my pain!

168
00:10:18,980 --> 00:10:20,560
What is wrong with you?

169
00:10:20,740 --> 00:10:22,320
I-I'm so sorry!

170
00:10:28,020 --> 00:10:30,380
You'll be okay, and I can help!

171
00:10:30,740 --> 00:10:31,681
Do you know how?

172
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:35,278
Back in the capital, there
was this toad oil I stole.

173
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:37,800
I mean, that I bought!

174
00:10:37,980 --> 00:10:38,997
Jess said you stole it.

175
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:40,720
No, I paid for it, silly!

176
00:10:42,380 --> 00:10:43,800
Whatever, I don't care.

177
00:10:43,920 --> 00:10:45,800
Watch what it can do.

178
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:49,440
It makes all the sword boo-boos go away.

179
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:51,440
Does it really now?

180
00:10:51,940 --> 00:10:54,000
Okay, let's hope this works.

181
00:10:56,060 --> 00:10:58,200
But I think...

182
00:11:01,760 --> 00:11:03,240
You should stay.

183
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:07,660
That food over there?

184
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:09,560
Oh, yes.

185
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:11,034
Allow me to serve you.

186
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:21,040
Who's this Gyukimaru? Ah, yes.

187
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:25,020
The man's a well-known figure.

188
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:28,040
He stands guard on Bandit's bridge.

189
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:33,120
I have reclaimed Shusui and returned
it to the only place that it belongs.

190
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:36,417
That fabed sword is a
national treasure that was

191
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:39,660
taken from the grave of the
legendary samurai, Ryuma!

192
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:43,357
No one knows who he is
or from whence he hails,

193
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:46,837
But whenever anyone carrying a
weapon attempts to cross that bridge,

194
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:49,508
then you can be certain
that he will appear.

195
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:53,086
So there's no need to
rush back and fight him.

196
00:11:53,260 --> 00:11:54,907
I'll go deal with him later.

197
00:11:55,820 --> 00:11:58,377
Well, I'm curious to
know more about the guy.

198
00:11:58,460 --> 00:12:01,477
I guess first I should learn more
about who's right in front of me.

199
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:04,560
Who are you and why was
that Grim Reaper after you?

200
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:18,280
In truth, we did something that
earned us the wrath of one Oshogun.

201
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:20,910
Oshogun, huh?

202
00:12:21,380 --> 00:12:23,980
That, uh, Orochi guy? Orochi.

203
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:27,140
Say, Mr. Samurai!

204
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:30,200
My name is Dock!

205
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:34,497
But when you put an O in front like other
girls' names, it sounds like I'm a boy!

206
00:12:34,580 --> 00:12:36,200
Isn't that so funny?

207
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:38,480
Nope. Not really.

208
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:44,829
But everyone laughs a lot when
I tell them, now why not you?

209
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:46,453
Because it's not funny.

210
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:52,781
I assumed from the way you dressed
that you were a samurai of Wano.

211
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:55,174
But it would seem you're from overseas.

212
00:12:55,300 --> 00:12:57,300
You don't look like a bad person.

213
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:02,820
You look very, uh, friendly. Liar!

214
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:04,160
I'm sorry.

215
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:07,517
On the outside, you look scary.

216
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:12,160
But I know you're nice because you
saved our butts when we were in trouble!

217
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:32,370
Mr.

218
00:13:32,453 --> 00:13:36,060
Samurai, I'm going to tell you
something that must remain a secret.

219
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:40,537
What is it?

220
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:42,897
I'm searching for my older brother.

221
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:46,820
We were separated 20 long years ago.

222
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:54,737
Also, I believe he may be
here in Wano right now.

223
00:13:54,820 --> 00:14:00,020
My brother's name is Kozuki Momonosuke.

224
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:03,060
I'm his younger sister.

225
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:08,260
And my name is Hyori.

226
00:14:13,620 --> 00:14:14,450
Momonosuke?

227
00:14:14,533 --> 00:14:15,379
You're his sister?

228
00:14:16,420 --> 00:14:17,600
Wait, you know him?

229
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:20,428
So my leap of faith
paid off, how wonderful!

230
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:23,840
Honestly, it was a big leap.

231
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:27,437
You've met my brother before, haven't you?

232
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:29,360
That must mean he's still alive

233
00:14:30,060 --> 00:14:31,397
Oh, hold on a sec.

234
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:33,340
I need to process this.

235
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:39,141
You know, I heard there's a movement
to bring back the Kozuki clan.

236
00:14:39,620 --> 00:14:40,517
Is that true?

237
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:42,757
Are you part of it? I knew it!

238
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,977
You're a friend of the
cause from a foreign land!

239
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:47,589
You're here to help my
brother, aren't you?

240
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:48,870
No!

241
00:14:48,953 --> 00:14:49,800
Wait, you're not?

242
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:51,140
Then who are you?

243
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:52,300
A foe?

244
00:14:53,980 --> 00:14:54,877
I'm an ally.

245
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:56,640
I can tell you that much.

246
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:00,654
Well, that's a relief.

247
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:04,047
What about the others, then?

248
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:06,575
Do you know if Kin'emon is still alive?

249
00:15:08,300 --> 00:15:12,020
And Kanjuro, Raizo, what of Kikunojo?

250
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:13,769
Are they with you as well?

251
00:15:14,340 --> 00:15:15,170
Kikunojo?

252
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:17,060
Oh, you mean Kiku, right?

253
00:15:18,140 --> 00:15:20,100
Yeah, one thing, though.

254
00:15:20,660 --> 00:15:22,340
I need some kind of proof.

255
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:25,200
How do I know you're really Momo's sister?

256
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:30,180
Allow me to explain.

257
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:34,497
Yeah, okay.

258
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:36,637
Guess it all adds up then?

259
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:39,177
Momo traveled two decades ahead in time.

260
00:15:39,260 --> 00:15:40,777
So he's still eight years old.

261
00:15:40,860 --> 00:15:42,917
And even though you're his younger sister.

262
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:46,060
You're 26 now since
you had to stay behind.

263
00:15:46,700 --> 00:15:47,530
Yes.

264
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:49,000
By the way?

265
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:53,557
Are you sure this twerp's
allowed to hear all this?

266
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:55,140
Yeah, it's okay.

267
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:57,040
I already knew about it.

268
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:01,280
She told me a long time ago.

269
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:04,340
It was a special secret
between the two of us.

270
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:07,039
Otoko is one of my closest friends.

271
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:12,220
Her smiling face has gotten
me through so many hard days.

272
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:15,140
She reminds me of myself 20 years ago.

273
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:17,980
I was about her age on that day.

274
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:21,880
The day my whole world fell apart.

275
00:16:22,620 --> 00:16:24,280
I'll never forget it.

276
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:30,720
Leave to the future.

277
00:16:31,140 --> 00:16:32,020
Live on.

278
00:16:34,340 --> 00:16:36,820
Please, I made up my mind, too!

279
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:39,220
Mother! Father!

280
00:16:39,660 --> 00:16:41,280
No, I won't leave you!

281
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:46,972
At the time, I had no understanding
of what was occurring.

282
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:50,040
Suddenly, right before my eyes,

283
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:54,506
My beloved brother and the others
all vanished into the flames.

284
00:16:57,140 --> 00:17:01,820
Before I could even process the death
of my father, I lost my mother as well.

285
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:05,207
Everything was taken
from me in a single day.

286
00:17:05,740 --> 00:17:09,034
I was told that my brother
would return in twenty years.

287
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:15,260
But after a tragedy so great, such an
immaterial hope offered me little solace.

288
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:19,260
I completely lost the will to go on.

289
00:17:21,360 --> 00:17:24,777
Why didn't they have you jump
into the future with your brother?

290
00:17:24,860 --> 00:17:26,620
It was either him or me.

291
00:17:27,240 --> 00:17:29,652
We couldn't let the Kozuki bloodline die.

292
00:17:30,100 --> 00:17:33,629
If something happened to both
of us, then all would be lost.

293
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:34,880
So that's why.

294
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:36,580
That's messed up.

295
00:17:36,740 --> 00:17:38,916
I was never completely alone, though.

296
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:40,200
My father's ally,

297
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:45,620
a kindly retainer named Kawamatsu the
Kappa, raised me with patience and care.

298
00:17:46,060 --> 00:17:47,320
A Kappa? Indeed.

299
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:50,857
Hard to believe that he's
one of those river creatures,

300
00:17:50,940 --> 00:17:52,940
but he's not ashamed of that fact.

301
00:17:53,260 --> 00:17:54,495
He takes pride in it.

302
00:17:55,300 --> 00:17:59,520
The day that the castle burned
down, we were surrounded by enemies.

303
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:03,780
However, he helped me escape
through the moat undetected.

304
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:06,660
Princess, just a bit longer.

305
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:12,380
After losing my father, mother,

306
00:18:12,640 --> 00:18:16,780
and brother, the shock robbed
me of my ability to speak.

307
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:19,820
but he did his utmost best to cheer me up.

308
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:22,620
Princess, this is the cup-a-dance.

309
00:18:30,800 --> 00:18:33,320
Surprise, I brought you food. Dig in.

310
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:40,844
Your tummy is saying it's
hungry, too, isn't it?

311
00:18:41,300 --> 00:18:44,760
No, I have a bit of an
upset stomach, you see.

312
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:47,104
That's why it's being so noisy.

313
00:18:47,580 --> 00:18:48,580
That's a fib.

314
00:18:49,360 --> 00:18:51,937
Can't you at least put
half of this with me?

315
00:18:52,020 --> 00:18:53,617
No, no, it's fine.

316
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:56,818
I found a grilled fish
swimming in the river earlier.

317
00:19:00,940 --> 00:19:03,980
A grilled fish was in
the water? Yes, indeed.

318
00:19:04,380 --> 00:19:07,380
I filleted and gobbled up
that tasty little fellow.

319
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:09,920
So don't you worry about me, all right?

320
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:13,560
He would always make sure to feed me,

321
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:16,537
even if that meant there
was nothing left for him.

322
00:19:16,620 --> 00:19:18,377
I owe everything to him.

323
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:21,417
His kindness allowed
me to smile once more.

324
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:24,853
If it weren't for his help,
I'd have been lost to sorrow.

325
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:27,260
So where is he now?

326
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:30,577
When I was about 13, we were separated.

327
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:33,560
Since then, I haven't seen him.

328
00:19:35,020 --> 00:19:37,200
However, he is a samurai.

329
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:40,115
Kawamatsu must be out there somewhere.

330
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:41,280
I know it!

331
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:45,777
Certainly he's waiting for the day of
the great battle to make his return.

332
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:48,980
How I wish to see him again,
as well as the others.

333
00:19:49,540 --> 00:19:51,760
I've never met a real Cape before!

334
00:19:57,080 --> 00:19:58,520
Sir Zorojuro? Hmm?

335
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:03,640
If I may ask you, who's here to
help prepare for the big uprising?

336
00:20:04,280 --> 00:20:05,560
There's a few of us.

337
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:07,620
What? What?

338
00:20:08,320 --> 00:20:11,940
So the doggie and the kitty
are with you as well? Yeah.

339
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:14,817
But I had heard that they were both dead.

340
00:20:14,900 --> 00:20:17,429
I was certain I would
never see them again.

341
00:20:17,980 --> 00:20:22,333
I don't think Cat Vipers arrived here
yet, but he's involved in the plans.

342
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:27,080
What's with that face?

343
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:29,500
I am just so happy.

344
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:46,077
I can't cry now I am a samurai's daughter

345
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:49,197
considering that the
doggy and kitty made it

346
00:20:49,280 --> 00:20:52,817
back all of the Akazaya
9 could reunite that

347
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:55,665
would be like a dream
well don't get your hopes

348
00:21:00,060 --> 00:21:02,000
There's Kin'emon,

349
00:21:02,340 --> 00:21:05,757
then Kanjuro, Raizo, Okiku,

350
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:09,660
Dogstorm, and Cat Viper.

351
00:21:13,700 --> 00:21:18,000
Those are the six we have contact
with, plus Momonosuke, obviously.

352
00:21:18,520 --> 00:21:22,457
But I've never even met the other
three, so who knows where they are.

353
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:25,658
One of them is Kawamatsu,
whom I just told you about.

354
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:29,560
The last three are him,
Denjiro, and Ashura Doji.

355
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:32,617
While I certainly do not know
where they are currently,

356
00:21:32,700 --> 00:21:34,820
I pray that they are alive and well.

357
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:40,460
But the entire flower capital is in
an uproar over this symbolic flyer.

358
00:21:40,780 --> 00:21:43,160
I am certain they know and will appear.

359
00:21:43,700 --> 00:21:46,917
Those are the flyers we handed
out to the rebels earlier, right?

360
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:47,980
Yes, they are.

361
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:50,277
Thanks to all this commotion,

362
00:21:50,360 --> 00:21:54,537
I'm sure the word has gotten out to
just about everyone you could imagine.

363
00:21:54,620 --> 00:21:57,000
But that's not exactly ideal for us.

364
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:59,677
Now the whole world
knows our meeting place,

365
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:02,417
and with all the arrests,
we're down a few men, too.

366
00:22:02,500 --> 00:22:04,340
That's looking pretty dicey.

367
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:06,426
Everything will be all right.

368
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:08,360
I have absolute faith.

369
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:11,830
Well...

370
00:22:13,380 --> 00:22:16,137
Too many men at the helm
always sinks the ship.

371
00:22:16,220 --> 00:22:19,697
I'm not going to sit here and
sweat the details. Exactly.

372
00:22:19,780 --> 00:22:22,637
We need you to relax so you can heal.

373
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:24,417
Besides, it's out of your hands.

374
00:22:24,500 --> 00:22:26,437
Now get some rest.

375
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:27,557
All right.

376
00:22:27,640 --> 00:22:29,300
No need to tell me twice!

377
00:22:32,580 --> 00:22:34,340
Otoko, can you believe it?

378
00:22:35,100 --> 00:22:36,880
My brother is alive.

379
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:39,897
Such good news.

380
00:22:39,980 --> 00:22:41,000
This is great.

381
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:44,600
I'm so happy for you.

382
00:22:46,020 --> 00:22:47,977
This is the best day ever.

383
00:22:48,060 --> 00:22:49,620
It really is.

384
00:22:51,700 --> 00:22:55,100
With all of this racket, I'm
never going to get to sleep.

385
00:23:01,120 --> 00:23:02,977
He's eight years old.

386
00:23:03,060 --> 00:23:04,260
Hard to believe.

387
00:23:05,180 --> 00:23:07,337
To think he's still but a child.

388
00:23:07,420 --> 00:23:11,500
They'll all be just as I remember
them from two decades ago.

389
00:23:12,260 --> 00:23:16,580
I wonder what will happen once I see
them all again, but that's selfish.

390
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:19,038
I should wait till the battle's won.

391
00:23:19,320 --> 00:23:21,920
I don't wish to distract. That's right.

392
00:23:22,340 --> 00:23:23,700
I should be patient.

393
00:23:25,220 --> 00:23:26,161
Don't you think?

394
00:23:49,620 --> 00:23:53,700
I wouldn't have thought there were
so many conspirators amongst us.

395
00:23:54,800 --> 00:23:58,180
All who are present, bear
witness to these traitors.

396
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:01,677
These are the faces of
those who dare to take a

397
00:24:01,760 --> 00:24:05,280
stand against Shogun
Orochi and Commander Kaido.

398
00:24:12,780 --> 00:24:13,780
Stop stalling!

399
00:24:19,380 --> 00:24:21,240
I do sympathize.

400
00:24:21,940 --> 00:24:25,237
You've been plotting this for
quite some time, haven't you?

401
00:24:25,320 --> 00:24:26,700
And you failed.

402
00:24:27,540 --> 00:24:29,437
Fukurokuju, sir, please don't do this!

403
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:30,840
We're all innocent.

404
00:24:31,120 --> 00:24:34,237
Why do you think these ankle tattoos
are a sign that we're criminals?

405
00:24:34,320 --> 00:24:36,100
This is but a popular design.

406
00:24:36,420 --> 00:24:38,477
We have nothing to do with any rebellion.

407
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:39,390
Is that so?

408
00:24:39,473 --> 00:24:43,200
Well, then, I challenge you to
explain the meaning of this flyer.

409
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:45,660
The implication is quite clear.

410
00:24:46,080 --> 00:24:49,557
Why else would there be a reversed
crescent moon at the center?

411
00:24:49,640 --> 00:24:54,560
No matter how you look at it, it spells
out insurrection against Shogun Oroji.

412
00:24:54,820 --> 00:24:57,380
It undoubtedly resembles your tattoos.

413
00:24:58,020 --> 00:24:59,780
You've caused enough trouble.

414
00:25:00,240 --> 00:25:02,260
Now accept your punishment.

415
00:25:14,420 --> 00:25:16,300
They're in some deep crap, huh?

416
00:25:16,600 --> 00:25:18,620
I hope nobody thinks we talked.

417
00:25:19,040 --> 00:25:22,940
They know we would never
rat them out, don't they?

418
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:27,100
Don't worry, you guys.

419
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:31,324
No matter what, Captain
Law will have our backs.

420
00:25:47,500 --> 00:25:49,560
Show us what else you got!

421
00:25:56,220 --> 00:25:58,920
I could go for a bit of sumo myself.

422
00:25:59,380 --> 00:26:00,980
The name's Medilloman.

423
00:26:01,780 --> 00:26:03,280
I'm a mess you up.

424
00:26:03,740 --> 00:26:05,440
I'm a gift or tell.

425
00:26:11,180 --> 00:26:12,010
Ah!

426
00:26:12,093 --> 00:26:13,486
Your body looks pretty tough.

427
00:26:13,900 --> 00:26:15,260
That I can work with.

428
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:16,980
You think this is fun?

429
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:19,940
These are loaded with
C-prism stone bullets.

430
00:26:20,100 --> 00:26:21,865
You won't be smiling for long.

431
00:26:24,020 --> 00:26:25,640
Come on and try me!

432
00:26:25,740 --> 00:26:27,140
That's over for you!

433
00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:30,540
It's over, he says.

434
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:33,800
This thing isn't over, not by a long shot.

435
00:26:34,580 --> 00:26:35,800
Keep it up.

436
00:26:37,960 --> 00:26:41,440
Oh, man, head to the right,
duck, and then jump up.

437
00:26:41,800 --> 00:26:43,220
Go to hell!

438
00:26:43,780 --> 00:26:44,740
Now! Sure!

439
00:26:45,500 --> 00:26:46,330
Ah!

440
00:26:47,720 --> 00:26:49,100
Get done!

441
00:26:49,560 --> 00:26:52,640
As instructed. Daniel! Then jump!

442
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:54,030
Ah!

443
00:26:54,400 --> 00:26:55,230
Ah!

444
00:26:56,540 --> 00:26:57,560
Ah! Ah!

445
00:26:59,560 --> 00:27:01,360
Ah! Ah! Ah!

446
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:04,470
Ah!

447
00:27:10,120 --> 00:27:11,300
Nice, old man!

448
00:27:11,520 --> 00:27:13,200
You pulled it off! What the?

449
00:27:13,460 --> 00:27:15,284
Are you able to see the future?

450
00:27:15,500 --> 00:27:16,520
That's amazing!

451
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:18,000
That does it!

452
00:27:18,180 --> 00:27:20,657
Look, I don't know what
trick you just pulled,

453
00:27:20,740 --> 00:27:22,975
but I'm done screwing around with you!

454
00:27:29,300 --> 00:27:31,940
Old man, head to the left! Huh?

455
00:27:32,220 --> 00:27:33,257
You're gonna die!

456
00:27:33,340 --> 00:27:34,320
Ha-ha!

457
00:27:34,420 --> 00:27:35,440
If you say so!

458
00:27:37,960 --> 00:27:39,380
Tricky old fart!

459
00:27:39,620 --> 00:27:40,855
How do you like this?

460
00:27:51,940 --> 00:27:53,120
Stop moving!

461
00:27:53,620 --> 00:27:55,091
You're playing in my ass!

462
00:27:58,660 --> 00:27:59,520
You're dead!

463
00:28:06,580 --> 00:28:08,960
You'll need to try a little harder.

464
00:28:10,020 --> 00:28:10,980
Ah, fine!

465
00:28:11,220 --> 00:28:12,360
How about this?

466
00:28:21,080 --> 00:28:22,500
All right, then.

467
00:28:22,940 --> 00:28:23,940
Let's roll!

468
00:28:24,500 --> 00:28:26,700
No contact! Right!

469
00:28:27,540 --> 00:28:28,370
Ah!

470
00:28:31,380 --> 00:28:33,237
All right, then. Let's roll!

471
00:28:33,320 --> 00:28:34,700
Oh, man.

472
00:28:34,920 --> 00:28:37,140
That was just normal armament Haki.

473
00:28:40,540 --> 00:28:41,370
Crap.

474
00:28:43,480 --> 00:28:44,860
Arm-a-day fire!

475
00:28:49,360 --> 00:28:50,400
That's not it.

476
00:28:50,580 --> 00:28:53,237
I still can't figure out
how I'm messing this up.

477
00:28:53,320 --> 00:28:54,150
Huh?

478
00:28:54,233 --> 00:28:55,391
Where'd you go to hit me?

479
00:28:57,720 --> 00:28:58,840
Alpaca Fancy!

480
00:29:00,640 --> 00:29:01,470
Hey!

481
00:29:01,553 --> 00:29:02,960
Which way should I go next?

482
00:29:03,580 --> 00:29:05,600
You listening, Mr. Straw Hat?

483
00:29:06,520 --> 00:29:08,140
Uh-huh, stop right there!

484
00:29:13,580 --> 00:29:16,140
Hold tight, it'll be easier this way.

485
00:29:16,320 --> 00:29:17,580
I'm so sorry.

486
00:29:18,700 --> 00:29:20,677
Let's do this thing, I'll pack a man!

487
00:29:20,760 --> 00:29:22,340
Oh, yeah, leave it to me.

488
00:29:22,960 --> 00:29:24,280
Put me down!

489
00:29:24,580 --> 00:29:28,000
I already feel awful over
how much trouble I've caused.

490
00:29:29,240 --> 00:29:32,580
Nah, I think the heavier I
am, the better, actually.

491
00:29:33,320 --> 00:29:34,150
Huh?

492
00:29:38,520 --> 00:29:40,167
It'll help with my training.

493
00:29:44,640 --> 00:29:46,580
You guys are really something.

494
00:29:49,160 --> 00:29:52,100
I must admit, this was a brilliant idea.

495
00:29:52,580 --> 00:29:54,933
Crystal clear and straight to the point.

496
00:29:55,880 --> 00:29:59,377
Even a fool like me could tell
what the two flaming birds meant.

497
00:29:59,460 --> 00:30:02,337
It's going down the day of
the fire festival at twilight.

498
00:30:02,420 --> 00:30:04,900
Then the meetin' place is Habu Port.

499
00:30:06,660 --> 00:30:09,580
Man, I gotta say, Kinama did good.

500
00:30:10,220 --> 00:30:11,580
How do you know him?

501
00:30:11,840 --> 00:30:12,700
Speak up.

502
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:16,520
Aw, what's with the long face, Shinobu?

503
00:30:16,740 --> 00:30:17,960
Cheer up, my dear.

504
00:30:20,100 --> 00:30:22,357
Well, I guess I really can't blame you.

505
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:24,793
I'd be pretty glum myself in your shoes.

506
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:27,740
The plan is coming apart at the seams.

507
00:30:28,020 --> 00:30:30,280
And the bad guys are in the know.

508
00:30:32,340 --> 00:30:34,537
Indeed quite regrettable, it is.

509
00:30:34,620 --> 00:30:38,517
It also grieves me to know
that our comrades bearing

510
00:30:38,600 --> 00:30:41,117
the tattoo have been
apprehended on our account.

511
00:30:41,200 --> 00:30:45,897
Ah, if only you could
claim it was all a lie,

512
00:30:45,980 --> 00:30:49,197
but then you'd mislead
your allies too well done.

513
00:30:49,280 --> 00:30:51,497
We're in quite the pickle here, aren't we?

514
00:30:51,580 --> 00:30:55,297
It's such a shame, I.

515
00:30:55,380 --> 00:30:58,321
I wish I'd known about
those ankle tattoos sooner.

516
00:30:58,880 --> 00:31:01,160
But tattoo or no, folks are watching.

517
00:31:14,200 --> 00:31:15,980
Ah, still no good.

518
00:31:16,180 --> 00:31:17,945
